{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791659308,"nonce":"8D5Pt8aQaW1XpA13N3kByt4Myrg=","title":"Images: img, background url() and svg, resampled to what they cover on screen","message":"blinc_ts has the parts of images and none of the whole: ImageResource (decodeImage, rasterizeSvg, resample), a renderer atlas with image slots, and the display list's image record, but a slot is uploaded once at a size the caller picks (SceneRenderer.setImage), nothing loads a source, and `img`, `background: url()` and svg do nothing. url() backgrounds are reported as unsupported (see ff2f7ff).\n\nashui draws each image resampled to the size it covers on screen (haxe/ashui/core/render/Images.hx, types/Bitmap.hx, ui/Image.hx): a pass over the display list's image records, each record carrying its slot and its on-screen scale, resampled into the atlas at a bucketed size (twelve steps an octave, at most 2048 a side), cached by slot, size and fit, the atlas emptied once when it fills; tiles are resampled once at their own size and repeated by the shader; an svg is rasterized at the size and tinted when it is a mask.\n\nPlan, each step committed with an offscreen pixel test:\n1. Renderer: resolve image records at encode time against a library of sources (slot = BASE + id * 4 + fit, below BASE the fixed setImage slots as now), resampling to the on-screen size, tiles, atlas reset. No CSS.\n2. `img`: load src (a path, a data: URL, http(s), a bundler asset URL), decode, size the element from the image when width or height is auto, object-fit, load and error events, alt text kept, `decode()`.\n3. `background-image: url()` with background-size (cover, contain, auto, lengths), background-repeat (repeat, no-repeat), background-position: parsed in blinc_abi, a Brush::Image applied by the addon, sources handed to the host to load.\n4. svg: `img` of an svg file, an inline `svg` element serialized and rasterized at its size, currentColor, and mask icons (`mask-image: url(icon.svg)` tinted by the text colour).\n\nOpen: where a source's slot is assigned (the addon, when it applies the paint, handing the host a list of sources to load), and how a changed src or a resize avoids reuploading every frame.","files":null}]}